CORE gnu-extensions
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ called: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
dropped the body
--
The line marker places the classes in a system header, where a conversion
failure in a body drops the body rather than reporting an error.
build_this_adjusting_thunk_body now passes a parameter of rvalue reference
type as static_cast<T &&>(a).  Reduced from libc++ 18 <functional>
(cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/test_functional.desc).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
